IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Goods and Services Tax Act 1993 (Singapore) -- whether I am liable to be registered (First Schedule paras 1, 1A, 1C(2), 16), by
-- when I must tell the Comptroller and from when I am registered (paras 4, 5), telling the Comptroller I have stopped (para 10),
-- objecting to a decision (s 49(2)), and what late payment, a late return, failing to register or an incorrect return can cost me
-- (ss 59, 60, 61, 62).
--
-- SEAT: the individual who makes, or proposes to make, supplies of goods or services in the course of a business in Singapore -- a
-- sole proprietor or a partner -- who may be or become a "taxable person".
--
-- Provisions covered: First Schedule paras 1(1)(a)(ii), (b), 1(3)(b), 1(4), 1A(1)(a), 1A(3), 1C(2), 4(1A), 4(2), 5(1), 5(2), 5(3),
-- 5(4) (as an input), 10, 16; s 49(2); s 59(1), (2); s 60(1), (2); s 61; s 62(1).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, version in force from 11 September 2026 (last amendment S 590/2026), as
-- deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/GSTA1993.txt.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the quarterly test for quarters ending before 1 January 2019 (para 1(1)(a)(i)); transfers of a going concern (paras
-- 1(2), 1A(2), 1B(2), 6, 7); VCC sub-funds (para 1(3A), (3B)); recipients of distantly taxable services (para 1B); the
-- Comptroller's anti-avoidance directions (para 2); end of liability (paras 3 to 3C); refusal of registration and conditions (paras
-- 4(3) to (5), 5(2A) to (2C), 7A); voluntary registration (paras 8, 9); cancellation (paras 12 to 14A); exemption from registration
-- (para 15); the Board of Review and appeals (ss 50 to 57); offences other than ss 59 to 62(1). No regulations under s 41 were
-- deposited, so when a return or payment is due is an input (the dates or month counts are given, not computed).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the individual's seat, with
-- the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT FOR PUBLIC
-- USE AS ADVICE. See NOTES.md.

§ `Goods and Services Tax Act 1993 -- what I must do, and what it costs if I do not`

§§ `First Schedule para 1 -- am I liable to be registered`

-- Para 1(1): "A person who makes taxable supplies but is not registered is liable to be registered ... (a)(ii) at the end of the year
-- 2019 or a subsequent calendar year, if the total value of all of the following in that calendar year has EXCEEDED $1 million: (A)
-- the person's taxable supplies made in Singapore; (B) if the subsequent calendar year is 2022 or later and the person belongs in
-- Singapore, the person's taxable supplies under paragraph 3(2)(b)(ii) and (3A) of the Seventh Schedule";
-- "(b) at any time, if there are reasonable grounds for believing that the total value of [the same] in the period of 12 months then
-- beginning will exceed $1 million".
-- Para 1(3)(b): not liable at the end of a calendar year "if the Comptroller is satisfied that the value of all of the following in
-- the next calendar year will not exceed $1 million".
-- Para 1(4): the count excludes "any reverse charge supplies of the person".
-- Para 1C(2): "supplies of goods or services that are capital assets of the business ... must be disregarded".
-- Para 16: values are taken "on the basis that no tax is chargeable on the supply" -- every figure below is before GST.
-- "Belongs in Singapore" (s 15) is the Act's own term, but its tests are not encoded; it is asked as a fact.
DECLARE `My year of business` HAS
    `I am already registered`                                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `my taxable supplies made in Singapore in the calendar year`             IS A NUMBER    -- before GST; no reverse charge supplies
    `of those, sales of my business's capital assets`                        IS A NUMBER    -- para 1C(2): disregarded
    `I belong in Singapore`                                                  IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 15, asked as a fact
    `my Seventh Schedule supplies under paragraph 3(2)(b)(ii) and (3A) in the calendar year` IS A NUMBER
    `the Comptroller is satisfied next calendar year will not exceed $1 million` IS A BOOLEAN  -- para 1(3)(b), the Comptroller's judgment

GIVEN `my year` IS A `My year of business`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What counts towards registration for the calendar year` MEANS
        `my year`'s `my taxable supplies made in Singapore in the calendar year`
    MINUS `my year`'s `of those, sales of my business's capital assets`
    PLUS  (IF `my year`'s `I belong in Singapore`
           THEN `my year`'s `my Seventh Schedule supplies under paragraph 3(2)(b)(ii) and (3A) in the calendar year`
           ELSE 0)

-- "has exceeded": exactly $1 million is not enough.
GIVEN `my year` IS A `My year of business`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I liable to be registered at the end of the calendar year` IF
        NOT `my year`'s `I am already registered`
    AND `What counts towards registration for the calendar year` `my year` GREATER THAN 1000000
    AND NOT `my year`'s `the Comptroller is satisfied next calendar year will not exceed $1 million`

-- Para 1(1)(b). "Reasonable grounds for believing" is a judgment, so it is an input beside the figure.
GIVEN `I am already registered`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
      `what I expect to count towards registration in the next 12 months` IS A NUMBER
      `there are reasonable grounds for that belief`              IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I liable to be registered now on what I expect` IF
        NOT `I am already registered`
    AND `there are reasonable grounds for that belief`
    AND `what I expect to count towards registration in the next 12 months` GREATER THAN 1000000

§§ `First Schedule para 1A -- if I belong outside Singapore and make Seventh Schedule supplies`

-- Para 1A(1)(a): liable at the end of a calendar year "if in that year -- (i) the total value of all the person's taxable supplies,
-- and supplies outside Singapore which would have been taxable supplies if made in Singapore, has exceeded $1 million; and (ii) the
-- total value of the person's Seventh Schedule supplies has exceeded $100,000".
-- Para 1A(3): not liable if the Comptroller is satisfied that next calendar year either total will not exceed its threshold.
GIVEN `my worldwide supplies in the calendar year`        IS A NUMBER
      `my Seventh Schedule supplies in the calendar year` IS A NUMBER
      `the Comptroller is satisfied next year will stay under either threshold` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I liable to be registered as an overseas seller at the end of the calendar year` IF
        `my worldwide supplies in the calendar year` GREATER THAN 1000000
    AND `my Seventh Schedule supplies in the calendar year` GREATER THAN 100000
    AND NOT `the Comptroller is satisfied next year will stay under either threshold`

§§ `First Schedule para 4 -- notifying and registration after a calendar year`

-- Para 4(1A): a person liable at the end of a calendar year "must notify the Comptroller ... of that liability within 30 days after
-- the end of that calendar year".
-- Para 4(2): "The Comptroller must register any such person (whether or not the person so notifies the Comptroller) with effect from
-- -- (a) the day immediately after the end of the month that follows the month in which the 30th day falls; or (b) such earlier date
-- as may be agreed". The 30th day after 31 December is 30 January; the month that follows is February; so registration runs from
-- 1 March.
GIVEN `the calendar year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I notify my liability for the calendar year` MEANS
    Date 31 12 `the calendar year` PLUS 30

GIVEN `the calendar year`                         IS A NUMBER
      `an earlier date agreed with the Comptroller` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`From when am I registered after the calendar year` MEANS
    CONSIDER `an earlier date agreed with the Comptroller`
    WHEN JUST `agreed day` THEN `agreed day`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        `add months` (Date 1 (DATE_MONTH `the 30th day`) (DATE_YEAR `the 30th day`)) 2
    WHERE
        `the 30th day` MEANS `By when must I notify my liability for the calendar year` `the calendar year`

-- A regulative form of the para 4(1A) duty. It is checked, not traced. Failing it is an offence under s 61(a).
DECLARE `Person` IS ONE OF `I`
DECLARE `Thing to do` IS ONE OF `notify the Comptroller of my liability to be registered`

GIVETH A DEONTIC `Person` `Thing to do`
`my duty to notify after a calendar year in which I passed $1 million` MEANS
    PARTY `I`
    MUST  `notify the Comptroller of my liability to be registered`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `I`

§§ `First Schedule para 5 -- notifying and registration on what I expect`

-- Para 5(1): a person liable under para 1(1)(b) "must notify the Comptroller ... within 30 days after the first day of that period
-- (the first day of that period called day X in this paragraph)".
-- Para 5(2)(a): registration "with effect from -- (i) where day X is before 1 July 2025 -- the day immediately after the end of the
-- 30 days; or (ii) where day X is on or after 1 July 2025 -- (A) the day in the second month (month M + 2) following the month
-- (month M) in which day X falls, that corresponds numerically to day X in month M; or (B) if there is no such day ..., the last day
-- of month M + 2"; or (b) "such earlier date as may be agreed".
-- Para 5(3), (4): where there are reasonable grounds to believe the threshold will be passed within the shorter window, "the
-- Comptroller may, if the Comptroller thinks fit, register the person with effect from and including day X". The Comptroller's
-- decision is an input.
GIVEN `day X` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I notify my liability on what I expect` MEANS
    `day X` PLUS 30

GIVEN `day X`                                           IS A DATE
      `the Comptroller thinks fit to register me from day X` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an earlier date agreed with the Comptroller`     IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`From when am I registered on what I expect` MEANS
    IF `the Comptroller thinks fit to register me from day X`
    THEN `day X`
    ELSE CONSIDER `an earlier date agreed with the Comptroller`
         WHEN JUST `agreed day` THEN `agreed day`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN
             IF `day X` LESS THAN Date 1 7 2025
             THEN `day X` PLUS 31
             ELSE `add months` `day X` 2

§§ `First Schedule para 10 -- telling the Comptroller I have stopped`

-- Para 10: a person registered under para 4, 5, 6 or 8 who "ceases to make or have the intention of making taxable supplies ... must
-- notify the Comptroller in writing of that fact and the date of the cessation, within 30 days after that date".
GIVEN `the day I stopped making taxable supplies` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I tell the Comptroller I have stopped` MEANS
    `the day I stopped making taxable supplies` PLUS 30

§§ `49(2) -- objecting to the Comptroller's decision`

-- s 49(1): "Any person may apply to the Comptroller, by notice of objection in writing, for review and revision of any decision" on
-- the listed matters (registration, the tax chargeable, input tax, assessments and others).
-- s 49(2): the application "must state precisely the grounds for the objection ... and must be made within 30 days after the date the
-- person has been notified of the decision ... or such other extended time as the Comptroller may allow". An extension is the
-- Comptroller's to give, so it is an input.
GIVEN `the day I was notified of the decision`      IS A DATE
      `a later day the Comptroller allows`          IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I object to the Comptroller's decision` MEANS
    CONSIDER `a later day the Comptroller allows`
    WHEN JUST `allowed day` THEN `allowed day`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the day I was notified of the decision` PLUS 30

§§ `60(1) -- paying late`

-- s 60(1): if tax "is not paid within the periods prescribed ... (a) a penalty equal to 5% of the amount of tax payable is added
-- thereto; and (b) if the amount of tax outstanding is not paid within 60 days after the imposition of the penalty ..., an additional
-- penalty of 2% of the tax outstanding is payable for each completed month that the tax remains unpaid commencing from the date on
-- which the tax became payable, but the total additional penalty must not exceed 50% of the amount of tax outstanding".
-- Simplification: the tax is taken to be wholly unpaid, so "tax payable" and "tax outstanding" are the same figure. Whether the
-- payment was made within the prescribed period is not asked: call this only for late tax.
GIVEN `the tax I paid late`                                       IS A NUMBER
      `I paid within 60 days after the 5% penalty was imposed`    IS A BOOLEAN
      `completed months unpaid from the day the tax became payable` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my penalty for paying late` MEANS
    `the 5% penalty` PLUS `the additional penalty`
    WHERE
        `the 5% penalty` MEANS `the tax I paid late` TIMES 5 DIVIDED BY 100
        `the additional penalty` MEANS
            IF `I paid within 60 days after the 5% penalty was imposed`
            THEN 0
            ELSE min (`the tax I paid late` TIMES 2 DIVIDED BY 100 TIMES `completed months unpaid from the day the tax became payable`)
                     (`the tax I paid late` TIMES 50 DIVIDED BY 100)

§§ `60(2) -- a late return`

-- s 60(2): if a return is not made before the prescribed period expires, the taxable person "must pay a penalty that is the sum total
-- of the following amounts, not exceeding in any case $10,000: (a) $200; (b) $200 for each completed month that the taxable person
-- continues not to make the return, commencing on the day immediately after the last day of the period prescribed".
GIVEN `completed months my return is late` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my penalty for a late return` MEANS
    min (200 PLUS 200 TIMES `completed months my return is late`) 10000

§§ `61 -- failing to register`

-- s 61: a person who fails to notify under paras 4, 5, 6 or 15 of the First Schedule or "fails to apply for registration as required"
-- is guilty of an offence and on conviction must "(c) pay a penalty equal to 10% of the tax due in respect of each year or part thereof
-- beginning on the date on which the person is required to make the notification or to apply for registration ...; (d) be liable to a
-- fine not exceeding $10,000; and (e) be liable to a further penalty of $50 for every day during which the offence continues after
-- conviction". 10% of each year's tax, summed over the years, is 10% of the total tax due over them.
GIVEN `the tax due since I should have notified` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my penalty for failing to register` MEANS
    `the tax due since I should have notified` TIMES 10 DIVIDED BY 100

GIVEN `days the offence continues after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most I can be fined for failing to register` MEANS
    10000 PLUS 50 TIMES `days the offence continues after conviction`

§§ `59, 62 -- an incorrect return`

-- s 59(1): a person who "makes an incorrect return by omitting or understating any output tax ... or by overstating any input tax" or
-- gives incorrect information "shall on conviction pay a penalty equal to the amount of tax which has been undercharged".
-- s 59(2): if done "without reasonable excuse or through negligence", "(c) ... double the amount of tax ... undercharged ...; and (d)
-- be liable to a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years or to both".
-- s 62(1): if done "wilfully with intent to evade", "(f) ... 3 times the amount of tax ... undercharged ...; and (g) be liable to a fine
-- not exceeding $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 7 years or to both". s 62(2): a proved false entry is presumed made
-- with intent to evade "until the contrary is proved".
-- Which limb applies is a finding for the court; the caller says which one was found. s 59(3) (input tax claims in a s 20(2A)
-- arrangement) is not encoded.
DECLARE `How my return came to be wrong` IS ONE OF
    `an incorrect return, without more`                  -- s 59(1)
    `without reasonable excuse or through negligence`    -- s 59(2)
    `wilfully with intent to evade tax`                  -- s 62(1)

DECLARE `What I face for an incorrect return` HAS
    `the penalty`                           IS A NUMBER   -- a multiple of the tax undercharged
    `the most I can be fined`               IS A NUMBER
    `the most months I can be imprisoned`   IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `how it came about`       IS A `How my return came to be wrong`
      `the tax undercharged`    IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `What I face for an incorrect return`
`What can I be made to pay for an incorrect return` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how it came about`
    WHEN `an incorrect return, without more`               THEN `What I face for an incorrect return` OF `the tax undercharged`,          0,     0
    WHEN `without reasonable excuse or through negligence` THEN `What I face for an incorrect return` OF `the tax undercharged` TIMES 2, 5000, 36
    WHEN `wilfully with intent to evade tax`               THEN `What I face for an incorrect return` OF `the tax undercharged` TIMES 3, 10000, 84
